From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:07:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/29] libcamera: software_isp: Gather focus statistics

The software ISP statistics carry an autofocus value, but nothing
computes it yet. Measure the contrast of the image while gathering the
other statistics: sum the squared differences between neighbouring
green samples, which grow as the image gets sharper, in a grid of 8x8
zones over the statistics window. Samples next to a saturated one are
left out, as clipped highlights spread when they blur and would make a
defocused image look sharper.

The zones let the IPA measure the focus over any part of the image, for
the AfWindows control, and with the sums of the green samples it can
normalise the contrast to the brightness so that exposure changes do
not look like focus changes.

The statistics functions get the line number, relative to the window,
to find the zone row. The added cost is one squared difference per
sample, on the frames statistics are gathered for.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
